(5433, 'Anti-oxidant vitamins in iron', '', 'Present study was designed to investigate the relationship of iron deficiency anemia with anti oxidant vitamins (Retinol, B-carotene, ascorbic acid and ?-tocopherol). Forty- three anemic subjects (19 males and 24 females) and twenty-five control subjects were included in the study. The blood was analyzed for hemoglobin, red blood cells indices, serum iron and total iron binding capacity. The results of these parameters were statistically significant (p<0.001) as compared to control subjects, but the levels of vitamins of anemic subjects were found to be statistically insignificant as compared to control subjects.', 'Sadia Afzal, Aziza Khanum, MSA Zuberi', 'l-6', 'Iron deficiency anemia, binding capacity, hemoglobin', 'http://www.localhost/pakjp/wp-content/uploads/pdfs/18/2/PJP-18-2-2001-1-6.pdf', 18, 2, 0, 1, 0, 0, '2001-07-01 06:00:00', '2020-01-27 07:55:15'),
